/ A window of its own for the browser on PlangOS's screen: a second Chromium, started with the running one's
/ profile, hands it a new app window on plang's own blank page and exits. The page it shows is the caller's to give,
/ over the running browser's pipe — never on this command line.
/ Trusted by origin (579), as Screen is: the program, its flags and environment are named here, with only the app's
/ own anchors %!app.AbsolutePath% and %!app.OsAbsolutePath%.
Window
- start terminal '//usr/lib/chromium/chromium' with parameters '--ozone-platform=wayland', '--no-first-run',
    '--no-default-browser-check', '--user-data-dir=%!app.AbsolutePath%/.browser',
    '--app=file://%!app.OsAbsolutePath%/system/browser/blank.html',
    with environment variables XDG_RUNTIME_DIR="%!app.AbsolutePath%/.run" and WAYLAND_DISPLAY="wayland-plang",
    with a clean environment, keep PULSE_SERVER and HOME from plang's environment,
    and wait until it exits (it hands the window over and ends)
